4. In addition to the cases of multi-purpose land use prescribed in clause 1 Article 218 of the Land Law, the Government is assigned to regulate other cases of multi-purpose land use.

5. Certain provisions on land information system:

a) The central budget shall ensure activities of the national land information system at the central level;

b) Local budgets shall ensure activities of the national land information system at the local level;

c) The State encourages qualified organizations and individuals to participate in providing services for building, managing, operating and exploiting the national land information system in accordance with law;

d) The engagement of services for operating and maintaining the land information system shall be carried out in accordance with laws on management of IT application activities funded by the state budget.

