Điều 4. Tham gia điều trị hoặc tư vấn tâm lý

1. Người làm công tác xã hội phối hợp, thống nhất với cơ sở khám bệnh, chữa bệnh hoặc tổ chức, cá nhân khác có liên quan xác định việc điều trị, tư vấn tâm lý phù hợp với lứa tuổi, giới tính người chưa thành niên.

2. Hình thức điều trị hoặc tư vấn tâm lý bao gồm:

a) Trực tiếp tại cơ sở khám bệnh, chữa bệnh hoặc tổ chức khác có chức năng điều trị hoặc tư vấn tâm lý;
b) Tại nơi ở của người chưa thành niên phạm tội tham gia điều trị hoặc tư vấn tâm lý.

target:
b) Cooperate with the direct supervisor in developing plans for the execution of decisions on the application of diversion measures involving participation in educational and vocational training programs;
c) Periodically assess the compliance status and learning or training results of juvenile delinquents participating in educational and vocational training programs on a monthly basis, or an ad hoc basis upon request, or when such juvenile delinquents violate relevant obligations, and send such assessments to the direct supervisor for reporting to the President of the commune-level People’s Committee;

d) Manage juvenile delinquents participating in educational and vocational training programs during their period of study at educational institutions or vocational education institutions;

dd) Upon completion of the education or vocational training period, issue a written evaluation of the learning or training results of juvenile delinquents participating in educational and vocational training programs and send it to the direct supervisor, or issue vocational training certificates to participants who meet the prescribed conditions.

Article 4. Participation in psychological treatment or counseling

1. Social workers shall reach an agreement and cooperate with medical examination and treatment establishments, or relevant organizations/individuals, in determining appropriate psychological treatment or counseling suitable to the age and gender of the juvenile.

2. Forms of psychological treatment or counseling include:

a) Direct participation at medical examination and treatment establishments or other organizations competent to provide psychological treatment or counseling;
b) Participation in psychological treatment or counseling at the place of residence of the juvenile delinquent.

