c) Support persons serving community-based diversion measures in ensuring their right to have a legal representative, to be treated equally, to receive full and timely information, to have personal privacy protected, to receive legal aid, and to enjoy preferential policies regarding health care, cultural education, career guidance education, vocational training, and labor applicable to juveniles in accordance with regulations;

d) Cooperate with socio-political organizations, families, and agencies or organizations where persons serving community-based diversion measures study or work during the process of education, management, assistance, and assessment of their compliance with community-based diversion measures;

dd) Make decisions on the replacement of the direct supervisor upon proposal of the commune-level police authority;
e) Issue certificates of completion of community-based diversion measures;

g) Organize preliminary and final reviews of the implementation of community-based diversion measures in its area.

2. The commune-level police authority, where persons serving community-based diversion measures reside, shall act as the focal point and advise and assist the commune-level People’s Committee in performing the tasks and powers prescribed in Clause 1 of this Article, and shall have the following tasks and powers:

a) Perform the tasks and powers prescribed in Clause 2 Article 73 of the Law on Juvenile Justice;

b) Propose that the President of the commune-level People’s Committee issues certificates of completion of community-based diversion measures;

c) Advise the President of the commune-level People’s Committee on notifying the authority that has issued the decision on the application of diversion measures of cases of suspension of the execution of decisions on the application of diversion measures;

d) Advise the President of the commune-level People’s Committee on developing plans for the implementation of community-based diversion measures within the first 5 days of the first quarter, conducting preliminary reviews biannually, and conducting annual final reviews of the implementation of community-based diversion measures;

