dd) Assess, classify, and include in assessment reports the performance and results of the execution of decisions on the application of diversion measures by the direct supervisor;

e) Cooperate with the direct supervisor in reviewing cases eligible for proposing early termination of the execution of community-based diversion measures.

3. Relevant agencies, organizations, and individuals shall have the following tasks and powers:
a) Perform the tasks and powers prescribed in Clause 3 Article 73 of the Law on Juvenile Justice;

b) Monitor the activities, sentiments, aspirations, advantages, and difficulties of persons serving community- based diversion measures to agree on appropriate educational and supportive measures;

c) Proactively report to the commune-level People’s Committee and commune-level police authority upon detecting signs or acts of violation by persons serving community-based diversion measures to adopt appropriate managerial and educational measures.

4. With respect to the execution of decisions on the application of diversion measures involving compensation for damage issued by the Investigation Authority or the Procuracy:

The direct supervisor shall cooperate with the competent civil judgment enforcement authority in ascertaining the results of compensation for damage; urge enforcement in cases where the juvenile delinquent, their parents, or guardians have not complied with regulations; and report the results to the President of the commune-level People’s Committee.

