1. Within 5 working days from the date of receipt of a decision on the application of diversion measures, the commune-level police authority shall prepare a dossier for the execution of such a decision.

2. The dossier shall include the following documents:
a) The decision on the application of diversion measures;

b) The decision of the Head of the commune-level police authority on the assignment of cadres;
c) The decision approving the list of persons supervising the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures in the area; the decision assigning the direct supervisor for the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures;

d) The record of notification of the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures;

dd) The written commitment to complying with obligations by the person serving community-based diversion measures;

e) The plan for the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures;

g) Documents concerning absence from the place of residence or change of residence of the person serving community-based diversion measures (if any);

h) Documents concerning violations of obligations by the person serving community-based diversion measures (if any);
i) The consolidated report on the results of completion of diversion measures;

k) The decision on early termination of the execution of diversion measures (if any);
l) Documents concerning extension of the period of performance of obligations (if any);

m) Documents concerning changes of diversion measures (if any);

n) Periodic and ad hoc reports;

o) The certificate of completion of community-based diversion measures;

p) Other relevant documents.
3. Where the person serving community-based diversion measures changes their place of residence, the commune-level People’s Committee assigned to execute the decision on the application of diversion measures shall issue a written transfer of the dossier to the commune-level People’s Committee of the place to which such person relocates.

