4. The handover of the dossier shall be documented in writing and kept on file as part of the dossier for the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures.

5. The commune-level police authority shall close the dossier in the following cases:

a) Suspension of the execution of the decision on the application of diversion measures;

b) The person serving community-based diversion measures is issued a certificate of completion of community- based diversion measures.

6. The preparation, registration, management, use, and closure of dossiers for the execution of decisions on the application of diversion measures shall be carried out in accordance with the regulations and guidelines of the Ministry of Public Security of Vietnam.

Article 10. Procedures for handling persons serving community-based diversion measures who violate

obligations
1. Where a person serving community-based diversion measures violates any of the obligations prescribed in Clause 2 Article 23 of the Law on Juvenile Justice, the direct supervisor shall cooperate with the commune-level police authority in preparing a record of the violation of obligations. The record of violation shall contain the following main contents:

a) Time and place;
b) Participants involved in the preparation of the record;

c) Full name, year of birth, gender, place of residence, the community-based diversion measures to be served, and the period of execution of the person serving community-based diversion measures;

d) Time of violation;
dd) Description of the violation;

e) Proposed form of handling;

g) Opinions of the violator;

h) Opinions of the representative of the person serving community-based diversion measures.

