b) Immediately after receiving the report from the direct supervisor regarding a violation of obligations by the person serving community-based diversion measures, the commune-level police authority shall submit a report to the President of the commune-level People’s Committee, enclosed with the record of violation and relevant documents (if any);

c) Immediately after receiving the consolidated report on completion of diversion measures from the direct supervisor, the commune-level police authority shall conduct an assessment of the results of fulfillment of obligations by the person serving community-based diversion measures, submit such assessment to the President of the commune-level People’s Committee, and keep it on file.

4. The commune-level People’s Committee shall carry out confirmation of reports and notifications as follows:
a) Immediately after receiving the evaluation and assessment report on the situation and results of the execution of the decision on diversion measures submitted by the commune-level police authority, the President of the commune-level People’s Committee shall confirm the report;

b) Within 3 working days from the date of receipt of the record of violation and the report on the violation of obligations by the person serving community-based diversion measures, the President of the commune-level People’s Committee shall prepare a dossier to request the authority that has issued the decision on the application of diversion measures to extend the period of performance of obligations or to change the diversion measures.

5. Criteria for assessment and classification of persons serving community-based diversion measures:

a) Excellent: Fully complying with obligations as prescribed in Clause 2 Article 23 of the Law on Juvenile Justice, and being awarded a certificate of merit or higher, or receiving written commendation or certification of commendation;

b) Good: Fully complying with obligations as prescribed in Clause 2 Article 23 of the Law on Juvenile Justice;

