3. Within 5 working days from the date of the working session with the juvenile reintegrating into the community, the commune-level police authority shall prepare the support dossier for the juvenile.
4. The preparation, registration, management, use, and termination of support dossiers for juveniles reintegrating into the community shall be carried out in accordance with the regulations and guidelines of the Ministry of Public Security of Vietnam.

Article 23. Termination of support for juveniles reintegrating into community

1. Support for juveniles reintegrating into the community shall be terminated in the following cases:

a) The juvenile reintegrating into the community has completed the period of community reintegration support as prescribed in Clause 2 Article 19 of this Decree;

b) The juvenile reintegrating into the community has changed their place of residence (with written notification and transfer of the dossier from the commune-level People’s Committee of the former place of residence to the commune-level People’s Committee of the new place of residence);

c) The juvenile reintegrating into the community leaves the place of residence, and their current whereabouts cannot be determined;
d) The juvenile reintegrating into the community has permanently settled abroad (with written confirmation by a competent authority);

dd) The juvenile reintegrating into the community is missing (with a court decision declaring the person missing);
e) The juvenile reintegrating into the community has died (with a death certificate or record certifying death, or a court decision declaring the person deceased);

g) The juvenile reintegrating into the community commits a new offence and is subject to temporary custody or detention, is sentenced to imprisonment and sent to serve the sentence at detention facilities, or is sent to a reformatory or a compulsory drug rehabilitation establishment.

