Article 7. Amendments to Article 37 of the Decree No. 162/2018/ND-CP

“Article 37. Power to make records of administrative offences
1. The persons having power to make records of administrative civil aviation offences include:

a) Persons having the power to impose penalties for administrative civil aviation offences, who have the power to make records of administrative offences in fields under his/her management, within the scope and contents of an inspection or examination;

b) Members of examination teams upon conducting inspection, who have the power to make records of administrative civil aviation offences within the scope and contents of the examination;

c) Persons of People’s Public Security Forces in the performance of their duties;

d) Civil servants and public employees of agencies whose heads have the power to impose penalties for administrative offences upon conducting inspection, examination, supervision, handling of offences or performance of their duties;
dd) Pilot-in-command, crew members assigned by the pilot-in-command to make records of administrative offences which occur on board aircraft in flight bearing Vietnamese nationality.

2. A pilot-in-command on board an aircraft in flight bearing Vietnamese nationality shall organize the making of records of administrative offences which occur on board aircraft in flight.

The pilot-in-command shall transfer a case of administrative offence committed on board the aircraft to competent state management agencies as follows:

a) The case of offence against regulations on assurance of aviation order and security shall be transferred to the aviation security authority at the airport/aerodrome where the aircraft lands;

b) Another case other than that specified in point a of this clause shall be transferred to the airports authority where the aircraft lands.”.

